}

— end example]

The restrictions on cv-qualification, and the manner in which the cv-qualifiers of the operands are combined to produce the cv-qualifiers of the result, are the same as the rules for E1.E2 given in [expr.ref]. [Note 1: It is not possible to use a pointer to member that refers to a mutable member to modify a const class object. For example,

