}

It is unspecified whether the value of f() will be true or false. — end example] — end note]

An immediate function is a function or constructor that is declared with the consteval specifier, oran immediate-escalating function F whose function body contains an immediate-escalating expression E such that E's innermost enclosing non-block scope is F's function parameter scope. [Example 9:

consteval int id(int i) { return i; }
